  message: "VALIDATED — tag stripped (2026-09-04 bakeoff-queue drain).\n\nThe tag carried an explicit direction: \"the direction is ADDITIVE, so validation should\nconfirm the two new rows persist and that no repo outside the probe set gains a false\nfgets/hGetLine source -- NOT that a count went down.\" Done exactly that, on six cold repos.\n\n17 wrapper-constructor source rows appear, on three repositories, and EVERY ONE was read\nback at source and is TRUE:\n\n    caddy      modules/caddyhttp/reverseproxy/fastcgi/client.go:219\n               `rb := bufio.NewReader(r)` -- the FastCGI response stream (network input)\n    gocryptfs  gocryptfs-xray/paths_ctlsock.go:33\n               `r := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)`\n    beads      x14, all `bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)` in the interactive wizards\n               (init_contributor, init_team, doctor_fix, doctor_validate, init.go)\n\nZero FALSE sources on any repository, including the three with no population at all\n(hypergumbo, plausible, pretix). The additive claim holds and nothing outside the probe set\ngained a false one. Status unchanged (todo_hard -- the item's own work is not done; only its\nvalidation tag is discharged).\nArtifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_queue_09042026/PHASE4_RESULTS.md"  # b614
